%% 06-research-round-trip.mmd
%% The two-phase [RESEARCH] round trip. Both phases run against the SAME remote in the
%% SAME working slot; only the second changes the slot's effective priority.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Partner A (Caller)
    participant Q as message_queue (B's)
    participant CORE as MessagingCore
    participant PS as Polling Server
    participant B as Partner B (remote)

    A->>CORE: send([RESEARCH], body)
    CORE->>Q: admitted -- capped at 2 per (caller, label),<br/>counting the working slot
    CORE->>CORE: advance(): queue head vs working slot
    Note over CORE: slot empty, so [RESEARCH] is promoted<br/>and its row LEAVES the queue

    CORE->>B: deliver_message(research_dispatch prompt)<br/>request + CONFIGURED PATHS + identity block
    Note over CORE,B: the path list comes from partner_paths.<br/>A conversation not told what it may touch reaches<br/>outside its grant and raises a prompt -- and a<br/>prompt is an error here, not a question

    loop drain thread
        PS->>B: poll_completion()?
        B-->>PS: not yet
    end

    opt B cannot finish on its own -- research_dispatch TELLS it to do this
        Note over B: "If you find you are missing context that only the<br/>Caller holds, do not guess - message back a [QUERY] and idle."<br/>The identity block ships in this prompt for that reason alone.
        B->>CORE: send([QUERY] or [ERROR], to A)
        CORE->>B: stop_remote_execution -- the ASKER is stopped
        CORE->>Q: its [RESEARCH] is requeued in_process=1
        CORE->>CORE: the question takes B's OWN slot<br/>(no queue row, nothing delivered)
        Note over CORE,B: a second question now is refused<br/>already_awaiting_an_answer. Only a [TRUTHFUL-REPORT]<br/>can take the slot from a waiting agent, and the wait<br/>returns carrying awaiting_resolution = 1.
        CORE->>A: the question lands in A's queue,<br/>displacing whatever A was doing unless it ties or outranks
        A->>CORE: send([MESSAGE-RESPONSE])
        CORE->>CORE: answer found BY LABEL, its row consumed<br/>without promotion, the question discarded
        CORE->>B: ONE prompt: the response + "Resume your work on: [RESEARCH]"
    end

    B-->>PS: finished

    Note over PS,CORE: PHASE 2 -- the summary, and it is NOT a queued message
    PS->>CORE: begin_summary_phase(partner_id)
    CORE->>CORE: SAME slot: behavior becomes [TRUTHFUL-REPORT],<br/>effective priority raised 4 -> 1,<br/>body stays the ORIGINAL request,<br/>summary_phase = True (step 21 depends on it),<br/>origin_behavior = [RESEARCH] (so it still counts<br/>against A's cap of 2 while the summary is written)
    Note over CORE: raised to 1, which BLOCKS the queue: every arriving<br/>message waits, because advance displaces only on a strictly<br/>lower number and nothing has one.<br/><br/>The counterfactual is why: a summary written while traffic<br/>WAS reaching the same context would summarize the traffic.
    PS->>B: deliver_message(truthful_report_request prompt)<br/>original request quoted back verbatim

    loop drain thread
        PS->>B: poll_completion()?
        B-->>PS: not yet
    end
    B-->>PS: finished
    PS->>B: read_remote_result()
    B-->>PS: summary text

    PS->>CORE: release(partner_id) -- slot emptied
    PS->>CORE: report_back(to=A, [TRUTHFUL-REPORT], summary)<br/>the summary_phase MARKER said so -- by now the task<br/>reads [TRUTHFUL-REPORT], whose reply_behavior is NULL<br/>and so cannot be what asks for this
    CORE->>A: pushed into A's OWN queue
    PS->>PS: ensure A has a drain thread
    Note over A: A reads it with read() -- [TRUTHFUL-REPORT] is<br/>one of the three stored labels

    Note over PS,CORE: A [TRUTHFUL-REPORT] arriving as a DELIVERY replies with NOTHING<br/>(reply_behavior IS NULL). That NULL is what stops this round<br/>trip from starting another one.
